    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Choosing an approach",
      "items": [
        "Mountpoint for Amazon S3 CSI helps when existing code expects files",
        "Direct AWS SDK calls give fine control over multipart uploads and conditional requests",
        "Hadoop S3A is the standard path for analytics engines such as Spark and Hive"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Permission design",
      "items": [
        "Take temporary credentials through IRSA or EKS Pod Identity instead of static access keys",
        "Grant least privilege per prefix in both the bucket policy and the IAM policy",
        "s3:GetObject must name the object path, as in arn:aws:s3:::bucket/*"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Common use cases",
